  "facts": [
    "René Konen Tunnel, 655 metres long, opened in 1998 to carry northbound traffic under Ville Haute, bypassing the city’s narrow pedestrian streets.",
    "At 100 metres, the tunnel bends right beneath the Chambre des Députés, then sweeps left, showcasing clever urban engineering.",
    "Named after former Minister René Konen on November 5, 1998, the tunnel honours his initiative that launched its construction."
